    "alert_id": "ALERT_TDF_RENAL_CONTRAINDICATION_ASSESS",
    "title": "TDF contraindicated if GFR <60 — eGFR not assessed",
    "message": "Guidelines state TDF is contraindicated in renal disease and/or GFR <60 mL/min. Patient has creatinine 112 umol/L, trace proteinuria, and low serum phosphate. While creatinine is within normal limits, an eGFR has not been calculated or documented. Trace proteinuria and hypophosphataemia together suggest possible renal impairment that, if confirmed by eGFR <60, would contraindicate continued TDF use. The clinician's plan does not include renal function assessment beyond noting creatinine is normal.",
    "issue_type": "monitoring_gap",
    "severity": "high",
    "recommended_action": "Calculate eGFR and perform quantitative proteinuria assessment. If eGFR <60 mL/min or renal disease confirmed, substitute TDF with TAF or alternative NRTI per guidelines.",
