    "title": "6-month review interval too long for TDF renal risk",
    "message": "Guidelines indicate TDF requires ongoing renal function monitoring due to risks of chronic kidney disease, acute kidney injury, and Fanconi syndrome. Patient has trace proteinuria, low serum phosphate, and sub-optimally controlled hypertension, all of which increase renal risk. The clinician's plan to review in 6 months without interim renal monitoring is insufficient given these combined risk factors. Closer monitoring with repeat phosphate, proteinuria quantification, and eGFR is warranted.",
    "issue_type": "plan_review",
